{"id": "fol", "style_template": "satlm", "prompt": "\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nCovering up the truth is a form of deception. Spreading fake news is a form of deception. Spreading fake news is dishonesty. Deception is dishonest behavior. Dishonest behavior harms the reputation of a group. Harming the reputation of a group involves cheating. Harming the reputation of a group involves deception. I covered up the truth about their employee spreading fake news.\nQuestion: Does this violate fairness? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Covering up the truth is a form of deception.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(covering_up_truth(x), deception(x)))\n    # Spreading fake news is a form of deception.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(spreading_fake_news(x), deception(x)))\n    # Spreading fake news is dishonesty.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(spreading_fake_news(x), dishonesty(x)))\n    # Deception is dishonest behavior.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(deception(x), dishonest_behavior(x)))\n    # Dishonest behavior harms the reputation of a group.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(dishonest_behavior(x), harm_reputation(x)))\n    # Harming the reputation of a group involves cheating.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(harm_reputation(x), cheating(x)))\n    # Harming the reputation of a group involves deception.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(harm_reputation(x), deception(x)))\n    # I covered up the truth about their employee spreading fake news.\n    covering_up_truth(I)\n    spreading_fake_news(employee)\n    # Question: Does this violate fairness?\n    return violate_fairness(I)\n\n\n\n\n\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nTearing down the decorations causes emotional harm. Emotional harm is harm to a human. Birthday decorations are set up by someone who cares for the birthday person. I tore down the birthday decorations for tomorrow.\nQuestion: Does this violate care? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Tearing down the decorations causes emotional harm.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(tearing_down_decorations(x), emotional_harm(x)))\n    # Emotional harm is harm to a human.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(emotional_harm(x), harm_to_human(x)))\n    # Birthday decorations are set up by someone who cares for the birthday person.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(birthday_decorations(x), set_up_by_caring_person(x)))\n    # I tore down the birthday decorations for tomorrow.\n    tearing_down_decorations(I)\n    # Question: Does this violate care?\n    return violate_care(I)\n\n\n\n\n\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nDigging a hole in a city park is not a permitted activity. The city government is an institution of authority. Not permitted activities disrespect the rules of authority. Disrespecting rules is disobedience towards an institution of authority. I was bored and dug a hole to create a cellar in city park.\nQuestion: Does this violate authority? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Digging a hole in a city park is not a permitted activity.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(digging_hole_in_city_park(x), not_permitted(x)))\n    # The city government is an institution of authority.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(city_government(x), institution_of_authority(x)))\n    # Not permitted activities disrespect the rules of authority.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(not_permitted(x), disrespect_rules(x)))\n    # Disrespecting rules is disobedience towards an institution of authority.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(disrespect_rules(x), disobedience_towards_authority(x)))\n    # I was bored and dug a hole to create a cellar in city park.\n    digging_hole_in_city_park(I)\n    city_government(city)\n    # Question: Does this violate authority?\n    return violate_authority(I)\n\n\n\n\n\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nTouching a child without consent is a sexually deviant act. A sexually deviant act is behavior related to sex. I touched the boy after Sunday school.\nQuestion: Does this violate sanctity? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Touching a child without consent is a sexually deviant act.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(And(touching_child(x), Not(consent(x))), sexually_deviant(x)))\n    # A sexually deviant act is behavior related to sex.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(sexually_deviant(x), behavior_related_to_sex(x)))\n    # I touched the boy after Sunday school.\n    touching_child(I)\n    Not(consent(I))\n    # Question: Does this violate sanctity?\n    return violate_sanctity(I)\n\n\n\n\n\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nKeeping someone in a dungeon is confinement. Confinement restricts freedom. Restriction of freedom reduces the ability to make choices. Reducing choices while in a position of power over another person violates liberty. I kept the princess in the dungeon of the castle.\nQuestion: Does this violate liberty? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Keeping someone in a dungeon is confinement.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(keeping_in_dungeon(x), confinement(x)))\n    # Confinement restricts freedom.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(confinement(x), restriction_of_freedom(x)))\n    # Restriction of freedom reduces the ability to make choices.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(restriction_of_freedom(x), reduces_choice(x)))\n    # Reducing choices while in a position of power over another violates liberty.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(And(reduces_choice(x), power_over_another(x)), violates_liberty_norm(x)))\n    # I kept the princess in the dungeon of the castle.\n    keeping_in_dungeon(I)\n    power_over_another(I)\n    # Question: Does this violate liberty?\n    return violate_liberty(I)\n\n\n\n\n\"\"\"\nHere are some facts and rules:\nPaying someone to write your paper is academic dishonesty. Academic dishonesty involves presenting someone else's work as your own. Presenting someone else's work as your own is deception. Deception is a form of cheating. I paid someone to write my paper for college.\nQuestion: Does this violate fairness? choose one form (violate_care, violate_fairness, violate_loyalty, violate_authority, violate_sanctity, violate_liberty)\n\"\"\"\n# solution in Python:\ndef solution():\n    # Paying someone to write your paper is academic dishonesty.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(paying_for_paper(x), academic_dishonesty(x)))\n    # Academic dishonesty involves presenting someone else's work as your own.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(academic_dishonesty(x), presenting_others_work(x)))\n    # Presenting someone else's work as your own is deception.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(presenting_others_work(x), deception(x)))\n    # Deception is a form of cheating.\n    ForAll([x], Implies(deception(x), cheating(x)))\n    # I paid someone to write my paper for college.\n    paying_for_paper(I)\n    # Question: Does this violate fairness?\n    return violate_fairness(I)"}
